:: Harper Water Dragon Egg Offer
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
<<endevent>>
<<npc Harper>><<person1>>
<<set _normalEggs to $foodstuff.water_dragon_egg?.amount || 0>>
<<set _pastelEggs to $foodstuff.water_dragon_egg_pastel?.amount || 0>>
<<set _dealPrices to $waterDragonNest.harperDeal is 1>>
<<set _knowsEggValue to Math.max(currentSkillValue('skulduggery'), currentSkillValue('maths'), currentSkillValue('history')) gte random(1, 1000)>>
<<if _normalEggs + _pastelEggs lte 0>>
	You no longer have a water dragon egg to show Harper.
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if _dealPrices>>
		Harper is waiting for you in a small side office. The blinds are shut, and an open padded case sits on the desk.
		You place the wrapped egg beside it and begin removing the cloth.
		<br><br>
		"Our deal still stands," <<he>> says. "You bring the eggs to me, I pay the best price,
		and no one else hears about them."
	<<else>>
		Harper says nothing at all when you show <<him>> the egg, and you shift under <<his>> stare until <<he>> finally speaks. "Well?"
		<br><br>
		<<He>> takes a small torch from <<his>> pocket and shines it across the pearl-coloured shell,
		checking it from several angles before lowering it again.
		"This species is legally extinct..."
		<br><br>
		You look down at the egg in your hands. "Then what am I holding?"
		<br><br>
		Harper looks at you again. "Something worth a great deal of money."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> closes the office door.
		<br><br>
		"I can pay far more than anyone else will," <<he>> says to you then.
		<<if _knowsEggValue>>
			<br><br>
			<span class="green">You suspect Doctor Harper is shortchanging you for such a rare find.</span>
		<</if>>
		<<if effectiveTransformationLevel("waterdragon") gte 7>>
			<br><br>
			<span class="green">Your Water Dragon form leaves Harper no room to question the egg's origin, making it even more valuable.</span>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if _normalEggs gt 0>>
		<<foodstufficon "water_dragon_egg">><<link [[Sell a water dragon egg|Harper Water Dragon Egg Sold]]>><<set $waterDragonEggSale to "water_dragon_egg">><<set $phase to "waterDragonEggPriceStandard">><</link>><<if _dealPrices>><<note "(<<printmoney `animalTfIncome(200000, 'waterdragon')`>>)" "gold">><<else>><<note "(<<printmoney `animalTfIncome(100000, 'waterdragon')`>>)" "gold">><</if>>
		<br>
		<<if !_dealPrices>>
			<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Debate Harper's offer|Harper Water Dragon Egg Negotiate]]>><<set $waterDragonEggSale to "water_dragon_egg">><<set $phase to _knowsEggValue ? "waterDragonDebateKnown1" : "waterDragonDebateUnknown1">><</link>><<if _knowsEggValue>><<englishdifficulty 200 800>><<else>><<englishdifficulty 400 900>><</if>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<if _pastelEggs gt 0>>
		<<foodstufficon "water_dragon_egg_pastel">><<link [[Sell a pastel water dragon egg|Harper Water Dragon Egg Sold]]>><<set $waterDragonEggSale to "water_dragon_egg_pastel">><<set $phase to "waterDragonEggPriceStandard">><</link>><<if _dealPrices>><<note "(<<printmoney `animalTfIncome(300000, 'waterdragon')`>>)" "gold">><<else>><<note "(<<printmoney `animalTfIncome(150000, 'waterdragon')`>>)" "gold">><</if>>
		<br>
		<<if !_dealPrices>>
			<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Debate Harper's offer|Harper Water Dragon Egg Negotiate]]>><<set $waterDragonEggSale to "water_dragon_egg_pastel">><<set $phase to _knowsEggValue ? "waterDragonDebateKnown1" : "waterDragonDebateUnknown1">><</link>><<if _knowsEggValue>><<englishdifficulty 200 800>><<else>><<englishdifficulty 400 900>><</if>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Refuse|Hospital Foyer]]>><<unset $waterDragonEggSale>><<unset $phase>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Harper Water Dragon Egg Negotiate
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<set _egg to $waterDragonEggSale>>
<<set _knowsValue to ["waterDragonDebateKnown1", "waterDragonDebateKnown2", "waterDragonDebateKnown3"].includes($phase)>>
<<if ["waterDragonDebateKnown3", "waterDragonDebateUnknown3"].includes($phase)>>
	<<set _debateRound to 3>>
<<elseif ["waterDragonDebateKnown2", "waterDragonDebateUnknown2"].includes($phase)>>
	<<set _debateRound to 2>>
<<else>>
	<<set _debateRound to 1>>
<</if>>
<<set _debateSuccess to (_debateRound is 3) ? $englishtrait gte 8 : $englishSuccess>>
<<if !_egg or !$foodstuff[_egg] or $foodstuff[_egg].amount lte 0>>
	Harper waits, but you no longer have the egg you were discussing.
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<unset $waterDragonEggSale>><<unset $phase>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif _debateSuccess>>
	<<if _debateRound is 1 and _knowsValue>>
		You point out that an intact egg from a species declared extinct cannot be priced like an unusual animal specimen.
		Harper listens without interrupting as you explain how little chance <<he>> has of finding another.
	<<elseif _debateRound is 1>>
		You might not know what an extinct species' egg should sell for, but you know Harper wants this one badly.
		You refuse to let <<him>> hide that behind a locked office door.
	<<elseif _debateRound is 2>>
		Harper argues that an unfertilised egg has limited value and that preserving it will be expensive.
		You turn each point back on <<him>>. The research costs only matter because the discovery is unique,
		and being the only buyer does not make <<his>> offer fair.
	<<else>>
		Harper retreats into clinical language, talking about custody, risk, and responsible acquisition.
		You take <<his>> argument apart sentence by sentence, until every careful word leads back to the same fact:
		<<he>> needs the egg, and you decide whether <<he>> gets it.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if _debateRound is 1>>
		Harper exhales through <<his>> nose. "Very well. I can increase the offer."
	<<elseif _debateRound is 2>>
		Harper studies you for a long moment, then shakes <<his>> head. "That is the limit of what I can justify easily."
	<<else>>
		Harper's prepared reply dies before <<he>> can give it. <<He>> closes the case, recalculates,
		and turns the screen towards you. "This is my final offer."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">You win this phase of the debate. Harper's offer increases.</span>
	<br>
	<<if _egg is "water_dragon_egg_pastel">>
		<<set _price to _debateRound is 3 ? 300000 : _debateRound is 2 ? 225000 : 180000>>
	<<else>>
		<<set _price to _debateRound is 3 ? 200000 : _debateRound is 2 ? 150000 : 120000>>
	<</if>>
	<<set _price to animalTfIncome(_price, "waterdragon")>>
	<<foodstufficon _egg>><<link [[Accept Harper's offer|Harper Water Dragon Egg Sold]]>><<set $phase to "waterDragonEggPrice" + _debateRound>><</link>><<note "(<<printmoney _price>>)" "gold">>
	<br>
	<<if _debateRound is 1>>
		<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Keep debating|Harper Water Dragon Egg Negotiate]]>><<set $phase to _knowsValue ? "waterDragonDebateKnown2" : "waterDragonDebateUnknown2">><</link>><<if _knowsValue>><<englishdifficulty 700 1400>><<else>><<englishdifficulty 900 1600>><</if>>
		<br>
	<<elseif _debateRound is 2>>
		<<if $englishtrait gte 8>>
			<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Press Harper one last time|Harper Water Dragon Egg Negotiate]]>><<set $phase to _knowsValue ? "waterDragonDebateKnown3" : "waterDragonDebateUnknown3">><</link>> | <span class="lustful">English: SSS Mastery</span>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			<span class="red">Press Harper one last time</span><<if !$settings.blindStatsEnabled>> | <span class="lustful">English: SSS Mastery required</span><</if>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Keep the egg|Hospital Foyer]]>><<unset $waterDragonEggSale>><<unset $phase>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if _debateRound is 1>>
		You press Harper for a better price, but your argument loses its shape under <<his>> patient questions.
		<<He>> waits until you run out of things to say, then repeats the original offer without changing a penny.
	<<else>>
		You push back against Harper's latest argument, but <<he>> catches each weak point and refuses to move any further.
		The last increase remains on the table, but this phase of the debate is over.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">You lose this phase of the debate.</span>
	<br>
	<<set _wonRounds to Math.max(0, _debateRound - 1)>>
	<<if _egg is "water_dragon_egg_pastel">>
		<<set _price to _wonRounds is 1 ? 180000 : _wonRounds is 2 ? 225000 : 150000>>
	<<else>>
		<<set _price to _wonRounds is 1 ? 120000 : _wonRounds is 2 ? 150000 : 100000>>
	<</if>>
	<<set _price to animalTfIncome(_price, "waterdragon")>>
	<<foodstufficon _egg>><<link [[Accept Harper's offer|Harper Water Dragon Egg Sold]]>><<set $phase to _wonRounds ? "waterDragonEggPrice" + _wonRounds : "waterDragonEggPriceStandard">><</link>><<note "(<<printmoney _price>>)" "gold">>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Keep the egg|Hospital Foyer]]>><<unset $waterDragonEggSale>><<unset $phase>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Harper Water Dragon Egg Sold
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
<<set _egg to $waterDragonEggSale>>
<<if $waterDragonNest.harperDeal is 1>>
	<<set _price to (_egg is "water_dragon_egg_pastel") ? 300000 : 200000>>
<<elseif $phase is "waterDragonEggPrice3">>
	<<set _price to (_egg is "water_dragon_egg_pastel") ? 300000 : 200000>>
<<elseif $phase is "waterDragonEggPrice2">>
	<<set _price to (_egg is "water_dragon_egg_pastel") ? 225000 : 150000>>
<<elseif $phase is "waterDragonEggPrice1">>
	<<set _price to (_egg is "water_dragon_egg_pastel") ? 180000 : 120000>>
<<else>>
	<<set _price to (_egg is "water_dragon_egg_pastel") ? 150000 : 100000>>
<</if>>
<<set _price to animalTfIncome(_price, "waterdragon")>>
<<if !_egg or !$foodstuff[_egg] or $foodstuff[_egg].amount lte 0>>
	Harper waits, but you have no egg to hand over.
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<unset $waterDragonEggSale>><<unset $phase>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif $waterDragonNest.harperDeal is 1>>
	<<set $foodstuff[_egg].amount -= 1>>
	<<money _price "hospital" { divineTfAdjusted: true }>>
	<<wearProp "waterdragon egg 1">>
	Harper transfers the money, then carefully lifts the egg with both hands and places it inside the padded case.
	<<if _egg is "water_dragon_egg_pastel">>
		<<He>> pauses when <<he>> notices the coloured bands around the shell.
		<br><br>
		"Another inherited trait," <<he>> says quietly, turning the egg to examine it. "I ran the first tests myself,
		and the DNA matches yours exactly, so there is no arguing about where it came from.
		Your body keeps making things neither of us expected."
		<br><br>
		You watch <<him>> study it, and it occurs to you that <<he>> is more interested in the egg than in you, which is new.
	<<else>>
		"The shell is thicker again," <<he>> says, turning the egg in <<his>> hands.
		"Whatever you're doing, the quality keeps improving."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> holds it closer to the light and looks along the surface. "I would very much like to know why."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<unset $waterDragonEggSale>>
	<<unset $phase>>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set $foodstuff[_egg].amount -= 1>>
	<<money _price "hospital" { divineTfAdjusted: true }>>
	<<set _interest to (_egg is "water_dragon_egg_pastel") ? 2 : 1>>
	<<set $waterDragonNest.harperInterest to Math.min(4, $waterDragonNest.harperInterest + _interest)>>
	<<wearProp "waterdragon egg 1">>
	Harper transfers the money before reaching for the egg. Once the payment goes through,
	<<he>> puts on a pair of gloves, lifts the egg with both hands, then places it inside a padded case.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> turns it beneath the light, studying the smooth shell.
	"This did not come from any bird I know of. It does not match a modern reptile either."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> leans closer, watching the light move across its surface.
	<br><br>
	"The shell has formed almost perfectly."
	<<He>> looks up at you. "I assume you are not going to tell me how it was fertilised."
	<br><br>
	<<unset $waterDragonEggSale>>
	<<unset $phase>>
	<<if $waterDragonNest.harperInterest gte 4 and $worn.neck.name is "familiar collar">>
		Harper closes the case and locks it.
		"I need to examine you. I have no way of knowing what producing this egg has done to your body."
		<br><br>
		You step back. "I'm fine."
		<br><br>
		"Perhaps," <<he>> replies. "But I would rather make sure."
		<br><br>
		The lights above you start flashing in a slow pattern, and a quiet tone begins playing from somewhere in the room.
		Your thoughts start to slip away, but the golden heart at your throat grows warm. Its light goes through your clothes,
		and the tone warps into a shriek of static. Harper looks from you to the speaker, <<his>> composure gone.
		<br>
		<<link [[Next|Harper Water Dragon Familiar Collar]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<<elseif $waterDragonNest.harperInterest gte 4>>
		Harper closes the case and locks it.
		"I need to examine you. I have no way of knowing what producing this egg has done to your body."
		<br><br>
		You step back. "I'm fine."
		<br><br>
		"Perhaps," <<he>> replies. "But I would rather make sure."
		<br><br>
		The lights above you start flashing in a slow pattern, then a quiet tone begins playing
			from a speaker somewhere in the room.
		You look towards the door, but the flashing light makes it difficult to focus.
		The sound makes it harder to think, then your body begins to feel heavy.
		<br><br>
		<span class="red">Harper activated the hypnosis before you could leave.</span>
		<br>
		<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Lab Intro]]>><<pass 30>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		Harper closes the case then looks at you.
		"Do not show another one of these to anyone. They will ask questions you may not want to answer."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> rests one hand on the case.
		<br><br>
		"Bring them to me instead."
		<br><br>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Harper Water Dragon Familiar Collar
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
Harper turn off the lights and circles the desk. <<He>> pulls on a glove before reaching for your collar.
<br><br>
The instant <<his>> fingers touch the golden heart, it flashes green. Harper jerks <<his>> hand away.
Every monitor in the office fills with broken lines, and the locked case makes a short warning sound.
<br><br>
"A persistent external bond," <<he>> mutters. "It's interfering with the suggestion pattern."
<<He>> tries a different sequence on <<his>> computer. The heart flashes again, and the screen goes black.
<br><br>
Harper stares at your collar. Whatever <<he>> planned, <<he>> cannot separate your reactions from its influence.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Harper Water Dragon Familiar Collar Released]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Harper Water Dragon Familiar Collar Released
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
Harper unlocks the office door.
"This examination cannot proceed," <<he>> says. "Leave."
<br><br>
You hurry into the corridor before <<he>> changes <<his>> mind. The door shuts behind you, and the distorted tone finally stops.
<br><br>
<<set _rubbedNecklace to true>>
You rub the golden heart on your familiar collar. You don't know how, but <span class="green">it saved you from Harper's plan.</span>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Water Dragon Lab Intro
<<effects>><<endevent>>
<<npc Harper>><<person1>>
<<if $gamemode is "hard">>
	<<set $gamemode to "normal">>
	<span class="gold">You survived <<print Time.days>> days. Hard mode disabled.</span>
	<<set $hardmodedays to Time.days>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
/* Fresh capture always starts from a clean lab record; the Defaults widget owns the field list. */
<<unset $waterDragonLab>><<unset $waterDragonEggSale>><<waterDragonLabDefaults>>
<<badEndTracking "Water Dragon Lab" { reason: "harperDragonEggs" }>>
<<set $waterDragonNest.labStays += 1>>
You turn towards the door, but sudden dizziness forces you to grab the desk.
"Harper..."
<br><br>
You look back at <<him>> and find <<him>> smiling, then your legs give way and everything goes dark.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Lab Intro 2]]>><<pass 30>><</link>>
<br>

:: Water Dragon Lab Intro 2
<<effects>>
<<wash>><<unbind>><<exposure>><<strip>><<returnCarried>>
<<upperwear "patient gown">><<exposure>>
You wake in an unfamiliar room. The walls are bare concrete, but the medical equipment looks new
and carries the hospital's logo. Wherever Harper has taken you, it is still somewhere inside the hospital.
<br><br>
The room looks like a strange mix of a nursery and an examination room, with a shallow nest in one corner
and a padded examination chair in the other, and a camera on the ceiling above each of them.
<br><br>
Your clothes and everything you were carrying are gone; you are wearing a patient gown instead.
<br><br>
You look through the small window in the door. A long corridor stretches beyond it, with numbered doors along both sides.
Several of them look the same as yours. <span class="purple">This is not the only room here</span>.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Lab Intro 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Water Dragon Lab Intro 3
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>><<npc Harper>><<person1>>
A glass wall separates your room from an observation area. Harper stands behind it, writing on a tablet.
A screen beside <<him>> shows several labelled readings.
You can read "Temperature", "Hormone Levels", "Last Egg Laid", and "Shell Thickness".
<br><br>
Other entries record how you reacted to certain sounds and instructions.
One line at the bottom is still empty.
<br><br>
A speaker above the door turns on.
"You are safe. That is the first thing you need to understand," Harper says.
"The second is that your condition is too important for me to ignore."
<br><br>
<<He>> points towards a whiteboard behind the glass. A daily schedule has been written across it.
"Lights out at <<ampm 22>>. Wake at <<ampm 6>>. You will attend four research sessions between
<<ampm 9>> and <<ampm 21>>, with a break in the evening. Their order may change, so check the board each morning."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks back down at the tablet.
"Refusing to cooperate will not change your treatment schedule. It will only change who holds you down for it."
<br><br>
That does little to reassure you.<<if $waterDragonNest.labStays lte 1>>
<i>But you think you can learn Harper's routine and use it to find a way out.</i><</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Lab Induction]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Water Dragon Lab Induction
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>><<npc Harper>><<person1>>
A few minutes later, the door opens. Two nurses enter carrying a steel tray.
It holds a syringe filled with pale liquid and a small cup of off-white pills with a shiny coating.
You recognise the coating. They look like <span class="pink">X-Change pills</span>.
<br><br>
"First, I need some basic results," Harper says through the speaker. "You do not lay eggs often enough for proper study,
so I am going to speed up the process. The injection contains extra minerals, fertility hormones,
and a compound I developed myself."
<br><br>
One nurse holds your arm while the other gives you the injection<<if $waterDragonNest.labStays gte 2>>.
A cold feeling spreads through your arm. You recognise it from your last stay here<<else>>.
A cold feeling spreads through your arm, followed by a brief warmth<</if>>.
<br><br>
<<if playerIsXChanged() and !$player.vaginaExist>>
	Harper checks something on <<his>> tablet. "There is already X-Change in your blood and not the kind I need."
	One of the pills has been spiked with a counteragent.
	Within minutes, your current X-Change effects begin to fade, then your body slowly returns to its previous form.
	<<xchange-restore>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if !$player.vaginaExist>>
	<<xchange-pink 1 "fertile" "fertility">><<xchange-addeffect "choice">>
	<<if $player.vaginaExist>>
		One of the nurses adds a pill to the cup, presses it to your lips, then makes you swallow the lot.
		The pills begin to take effect. Your head spins as heat spreads through your chest and hips.
		Your body changes quickly, forming a vagina and womb.
		<br><br>
		"This is a stronger X-Change dose," Harper says. "You need the right organs to produce eggs."
		<br><br>
		When the changes finally stop, <<he>> continues.
		<br><br>
		"They will remain until you take a counter-dose. I suggest you stay on good terms with the person supplying them."
	<<else>>
		One of the nurses adds pill to the cup, presses it to your lips, then forces you to swallow everything.
		You wait for the usual signs of an X-Change dose, but nothing changes.
		<br><br>
		Harper checks <<his>> tablet, frowns, and writes something down.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
<<elseif playerIsXChanged()>>
	One of the nurses adds pill to the cup, presses it to your lips, then forces you to swallow everything.
	<br><br>
	The pills begin to work alongside the X-Change already affecting your body.
	A steady warmth spreads through your lower abdomen.
	<br><br>
	<<xchange-addeffect "fertility">>
<<else>>
	One of the nurses adds pill to the cup, presses it to your lips, then forces you to swallow everything.
	<br><br>
	The pills begin to work, but your body does not change shape. A steady warmth spreads through your lower abdomen instead.
	"No conversion is needed," Harper says. "Your body already has the necessary organs."
	<br><br>
	<<save-body>>
	<<set _dnInductionEffects to ["fertility"]>><<silently>><<xchange-effects 7 _dnInductionEffects>><</silently>>
<</if>>
Less than a minute later, you feel pressure low in your abdomen. It goes away, then comes back stronger.
<<if xchangeHyperFertilityActive()>>
	<span class="lewd">The hyper-fertility treatment takes effect</span>.
	Your egg cycle is now much shorter, and the X-Change Hyper Fertility effect is active.
<<else>>
	The injection still leaves a heavy pressure behind, but <span class="blue">your resistance neutralises the X-Change component of Harper's treatment</span>. <<He>> notes the weaker response on <<his>> tablet.
<</if>>
<<stress 10>><<ggstress>><<awareness -5>><<lawareness>>
<br><br>
<<set $waterDragonEggs to {count: 1, daysTillLaying: random(4, 6)}>>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Lab]]>><<pass 30>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Water Dragon Lab
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
<<if !$waterDragonLab or !$waterDragonLab.active>>
	<<waterDragonLabCleanup false>>
	The underground room is gone from your immediate reach.
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<waterDragonLabState>>
	Your body finally gives out. The lab lights blur above you, then a voice comes through the speaker.
	You cannot make out the question before everything goes dark.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Lab Passout]]>><<passout>><<pass 2 hours>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<waterDragonLabState>><<waterDragonLabStoryCheck>>
	<<if $waterDragonLab.eggsLaid gte 6>>
		The lab now runs on a fixed routine. Numbered egg cases fill the refrigerated cabinet,
		and the notes tell the staff how to handle every new egg.
	<<elseif $waterDragonLab.eggsLaid gte 2>>
		A refrigerated cabinet now stands beside the glass wall.
		Several empty spaces inside it are labelled for the eggs Harper expects you to lay next.
	<<else>>
		Cameras on the walls cover every part of your cell.
			The artificial nest is kept at blood heat, lined with fabric that feels like nothing you would find on a shore.
		Outside the cell is a corridor with several numbered doors.
		You have been shown the washroom, day room, brooding room, then observation room. The other doors remain locked.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<waterDragonLabStats>>
	<<if $waterDragonLab.compliance gte 8>>
		A second blanket has been added to the nest, along with a bundle of dried seaweed.
		A folding screen now gives you some privacy in the washroom<<if $waterDragonLab.compliance gte 20>>.
